{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הארצות האל", :translit "ha-artzot ha-eil", :gloss "these lands"} {:he "ל\"א מלכים", :translit "lamed-alef melakhim", :gloss "thirty-one kings"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word הארצות read as allusion to 31 kings"}], :frame {:text "Joshua 12:7-24 enumerates thirty-one kings conquered by Joshua west of the Jordan. The lands promised to Isaac's descendants thus encompass the territories of these thirty-one kings listed in Joshua 12:24.", :sources ["Joshua 12:24"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הארצת", :translit "ha-artzat", :gloss "the land of"} {:he "וי\"ו", :translit "vav", :gloss "vav"} {:he "ו' דורות", :translit "vav dorot", :gloss "six generations"} {:he "יצחק יעקב לוי קהת עמרם משה", :translit "yitzchak ya'akov levi kehat amram moshe", :gloss "Isaac Jacob Levi Kehat Amram Moses"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling הארצת (missing vav) corresponds to six generations from Isaac to Moses, after which the full land is given"}], :frame {:text "Exodus 6:16-20 traces the lineage from Levi to Moses across four generations (Levi, Kehat, Amram, Moses); including Isaac and Jacob yields six generations from the patriarch to Moses, to whom the land promise is realized. Genesis 26:3 records the promise of these lands to Isaac.", :sources ["Genesis 26:3" "Exodus 6:16" "Exodus 6:18" "Exodus 6:20"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word הארצות read as allusion to 31 kings", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling הארצת (missing vav) corresponds to six generations from Isaac to Moses, after which the full land is given", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:08:11.425414753Z", :model "glm-5.2"}